# it_IT-serena-medium — Piper voice (Italian)

Custom Italian voice for [Piper](https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl), trained from the
`committa/serena-synthetic-it-28h` dataset (Qwen3-TTS synthetic voice).

- Language: Italian (`it`) — neutral Standard Italian (no regional accent)
- Voice: **Female** ("Serena")
- Sample rate: 22050 Hz
- Quality: medium
- Files: `it_IT-serena-medium.onnx` + `it_IT-serena-medium.onnx.json` (must stay together)

## Voice provenance

This voice model was trained using the
[serena-synthetic-it-28h dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/committa/serena-synthetic-it-28h).

The dataset audio was synthetically generated using Qwen3-TTS. A short synthetic reference clip was first generated with the default Serena speaker in Qwen3-TTS CustomVoice. This clip was then used as a fixed reference with Qwen3-TTS Base in voice-cloning (ICL) mode to generate the dataset samples.

The dataset author did not record or directly use recordings of real people as reference audio. The provenance and consent status of any underlying voice recordings potentially used in Qwen3-TTS training have not been independently verified.

## Recommended inference settings

The `.onnx.json` already embeds these defaults; the CLI uses them automatically.
They were chosen after stability testing: the Piper stock defaults (0.667 / 0.8)
tend to swallow phonemes (e.g. /r/ in "portato").

| Parameter       | Value |
|-----------------|-------|
| noise_scale     | 0.6   |
| length_scale    | 1.0   |
| noise_w         | 0.4   |
| sentence_silence| 0.2   |

